Subject: [PATCH 10/10] vectorize: generator-map packed loop for induction-only
 byte stores

Recognize the counted loop `for (i = C0; i < N; ++i) dst[i] = (u8)F(i)`
where F is a pure chain of 32/64-bit integer ops over i and constants
(no source loads). The packed map vectorizer requires a load and declined
these loops, leaving the histogram, byte_load and ASCII initializers
scalar. The transform (vectorize_generator_map.rs) runs AVX2-only, before
the CFG snapshot, and keeps a scalar tail.

Design and soundness:
- Lanes: 4 ymm vectors x 8 dwords cover 32 consecutive i. The lane
  offsets are chosen so packuswb(packssdw, packssdw) emits the bytes in
  element order, so no cross-lane permute is needed.
- Only ops that commute with truncation mod 2^32 are admitted (Add, Sub,
  Mul, And, Or, Xor, Shl<32); LShr only at U32. N <= 2^32 is enforced.
- Constants: loop bounds and shift counts use an exact conversion that
  rejects I128 values outside i64. IrConst::to_i64 truncates them, which
  would silently change a trip count. Arithmetic constants keep the
  truncating form, whose low 32 bits are exact.
- The matcher is read-only. Lowering is pure and only a complete lowering
  is committed, so a shape that fails late leaves the function untouched.
- The next value id is taken from the lowering's final counter. Using the
  starting counter reused ids and miscompiled (caught by the gate as a
  segfault before this commit).

Policy: the kill switch CCC_NO_GENERATOR_MAP, the LCCC_FORCE_SSE2 gate and
the [VEC-GEN] trace are resolved once in run_passes and handed to the
vectorizer through a setter, following the existing map switches. This
keeps the env-read ratchet at its budget. The function split keeps
fns_over_300 at its baseline. The kill switch is documented in
docs/optimization-passes.md. The census baseline is re-baselined for the
single new knob literal (knob_literals 500 -> 501, knobs_undocumented
unchanged).

Gate: tests/regression/check_generator_map.sh (self-checking kernels
a-g against gcc-16; fired=6 on the default path; zero with the kill
switch). Wired into ci_local.sh and the hosted ci.yml (gate parity).

Measured, Callgrind dynamic Ir, 45-benchmark corpus, vs upstream main
e8ae10ab (tests/benchmark, callgrind_corpus.py, 45/45 complete):
  histogram                  0.601455  (-40%; gcc-16 reference: 1.69M Ir)
  byte_load_reassembly       0.999499  (init loop only; reduction still open)
  zlib_ng_adler32_combine    0.999915
  geometric mean             0.987094  (was 0.998323 before this commit)
Same-binary control (lccc-genmap-8 vs the CCC_NO_GENERATOR_MAP=1 run of the
same binary): GM 0.988753, the same three benchmarks, so the attribution to
the transform is exact. The other changes against main come from earlier
commits on this branch.

Cost, stated plainly: the Godbolt static whole-TU instruction survey counts
the packed loop as code. On the same three benchmarks the static count rises
(histogram 64 -> 144, byte_load 153 -> 237, zlib adler32_combine 297 -> 380),
and that survey's GM moves 1.0601 -> 1.0959. The survey is documented as
size data, not a runtime gate (docs/GODBOLT_ORACLE.md); the Callgrind
